 - **Found on:** [Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity](../../dm/games/01002B00111A2000/README.md).
 - **Check:** `make -C dm/host/tests GAME=<id> audren-work` checks independently obtained Horizon sizing fixtures, both public parameter layouts, uninitialized padding, unsupported revisions, nested opens, undersized buffers, failure cleanup, caller-owned storage and close lifetime. The sizing implementation also matched 360 seeded parameter sets executed through Horizon's original machine code across REV1–REV15. The game note records the original-heap reproduction and audio check.
 
+### The renderer refills a short output queue
+
+- **Symptom:** crunching or crackle behind the music for many minutes at a time, then gone after a route change (headphones in or out). The log's `audio #N device callbacks` lines read `1.0 blocks queued on average at callback` with 20 to 36 underruns in every 2000 callbacks, where the rest of the run reads `4.0` and 0; `audren: renderer N rendered` keeps pace with the callbacks, and the render time stays well under 1 ms.
+- **Cause:** the render thread keeps at least 4.5 ms between renders once its four blocks are out (`RENDER_MIN_NS`), only 0.5 ms below the 5 ms a block plays for. With all four blocks queued it renders as each one comes back, so the gap never matters. Once a hiccup has taken the queue down to one block, the renderer runs on its own clock, and a timed wait that wakes 0.5 ms late or more each time makes it exactly as fast as the sound card: the queue never fills again, and each later wake-up costs a zero-filled callback. Nothing in the run lifts it back except a stretch with no callbacks (a route change, a long frame that holds the card).
+- **Fix:** once fewer than two blocks are queued (`dm_pcmout_queued`), `render_main` renders 2.5 ms apart (`RENDER_REFILL_NS`, twice the sound card's rate) until all four are queued again, then goes back to 4.5 ms. The log says so the first three times (`the output is down to fewer than 2 blocks`). `DM_AUDREN_REFILL=0` keeps 4.5 ms throughout, for an A/B run.
+- **Check:** `t_audren_layout --refill` runs the render loop on simulated time against a 240-frame sound card, with every timed wait waking 0.6 ms late and the render thread held 20 ms at block 200: with `DM_AUDREN_REFILL=0`, 0.98 blocks queued on average from 2 s on and 32 underruns there (the run's 1.0 and 1.4% underruns); with the refill, 4.00 blocks and none, after 3 renders at the refill gap. The cadence runs at 256 and 512 frames still play every block in order with no underruns. Not checked: a windowed run that reaches the short state on its own (it came twice in two of Tom's Ocarina sessions, an hour in, once after Quick settings and once in plain play).
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md) (Switch 2, MacBook Pro speakers at 240 frames a callback): 25 minutes of crunching in the Water Temple, cleared when the sound moved to AirPods.
